---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  SelectCompositions,
  SelectGroups,
  SelectPlayground,
  SelectRichItems,
  SelectSizes,
  SelectStates,
  SelectValues,
} from "../../components/SelectDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Select"
  description="Pick one value from a short list, in forms, filters, and toolbars."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Select</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A button that opens a list of choices and shows the one you picked. Use it
    for forms, filters, pagination, and compact toolbars. The chosen item lines
    up over the trigger, arrow keys move through the list, and typing jumps to a
    match.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="select-demo"><SelectPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Select usage"
      code={`import {
  Select,
  SelectContent,
  SelectItem,
  SelectTrigger,
  SelectValue,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/select";

const durations = [
  { value: "30", label: "30 minutes" },
  { value: "60", label: "1 hour" },
  { value: "90", label: "90 minutes" },
];

<label htmlFor="event-duration">Duration</label>
<Select items={durations} value={duration} onValueChange={setDuration}>
  <SelectTrigger id="event-duration" width="full">
    <SelectValue />
  </SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>
    {durations.map((item) => (
      <SelectItem key={item.value} value={item.value}>
        {item.label}
      </SelectItem>
    ))}
  </SelectContent>
</Select>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>items</code> (an array of <code>{"{ value, label }"}</code> or a
      record) so <code>SelectValue</code> can show the label for the stored value.
      Name the trigger with a <code>label htmlFor</code> or with <code
        >aria-label</code
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes and widths</h2>
    <p>
      <code>size="default"</code> (32px) is for forms and access rows. <code
        >size="sm"</code
      > (28px, small text) is for pagination, filters, and docks. <code
        >size="calendar"</code
      > is 32px with small text for calendar headers. <code>width="full"</code>
      fills the field; <code>width="fit"</code> (the default) sizes to the value.
      On touch screens every trigger and item is at least 44px tall.
    </p>
    <SelectSizes client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Values and placeholders</h2>
    <p>
      An empty string is a real value, so “Any type” or “Workspace default” can
      be chosen. Use <code>placeholder</code> when the value is <code>null</code
      >. Children on <code>SelectValue</code> replace the label, for example a name
      looked up from an id. Values can be numbers too, as in the rows-per-page control
      above.
    </p>
    <SelectValues client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Groups and separators</h2>
    <p>
      Wrap related items in <code>SelectGroup</code> with a <code
        >SelectLabel</code
      >. Use <code>SelectSeparator</code> to set apart an item, like one that is not
      available on this plan.
    </p>
    <SelectGroups client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Icons and rich items</h2>
    <p>
      Items can hold an icon or two lines of text. Long text wraps in the list
      and is cut off with an ellipsis in the trigger. Disabled items can be
      reached with arrow keys but can’t be chosen.
    </p>
    <SelectRichItems client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>disabled</code> on <code>Select</code> while a list loads, while work
      runs, or when it is empty, and add <code>aria-busy</code> to the trigger while
      loading. Set <code>aria-invalid</code> and point <code
        >aria-describedby</code
      > at the error. With <code>required</code> and <code>name</code>, the
      value is sent with the form, the form won’t submit without it, and a
      disabled <code>fieldset</code> disables the select.
    </p>
    <SelectStates client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In toolbars and overlays</h2>
    <p>
      Small selects sit in filter bars and inline in a sentence. Lists open
      above popovers and sheets. A trigger can be passed to <code
        >TooltipTrigger</code
      > through <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <SelectCompositions client:load />
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Select with a tooltip"
      code={`<Select value={mode} onValueChange={setMode}>
  <Tooltip>
    <TooltipTrigger render={<SelectTrigger size="sm" aria-label="Chat mode" />}>
      <SelectValue>{mode === "plan" ? "Plan" : "Normal"}</SelectValue>
    </TooltipTrigger>
    <TooltipContent>
      Normal acts on your request. Plan only proposes steps first.
    </TooltipContent>
  </Tooltip>
  <SelectContent>
    <SelectItem value="normal">Normal</SelectItem>
    <SelectItem value="plan">Plan only</SelectItem>
  </SelectContent>
</Select>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="select-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>Select</code> is the Base UI select root. It takes <code>value</code
      >, <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onValueChange</code>, <code
        >items</code
      >, <code>disabled</code>, <code>required</code>, <code>name</code>, and
      every other root prop.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SelectTrigger</code> takes <code>size</code> (<code>"default"</code
      >,
      <code>"sm"</code>, or <code>"calendar"</code>) and <code>width</code> (<code
        >"fit"</code
      > or <code>"full"</code>), plus <code>id</code>, <code>aria-*</code>, and
      <code>render</code>. It passes through field props such as <code
        >aria-invalid</code
      >, <code>aria-required</code>, and <code>aria-describedby</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SelectContent</code> renders its own portal, positioner, list, and scroll
      arrows. It takes <code>side</code> (bottom), <code>align</code>
      (center), <code>sideOffset</code> (4), <code>alignOffset</code> (0), <code
        >alignItemWithTrigger</code
      > (true), <code>collisionPadding</code> (8), and <code>container</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SelectValue</code>, <code>SelectItem</code>, <code>SelectGroup</code
      >, <code>SelectLabel</code>, <code>SelectSeparator</code>, <code
        >SelectScrollUpButton</code
      >, and <code>SelectScrollDownButton</code> wrap the Base UI parts and take their
      props. Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger is a combobox with <code>aria-expanded</code>. Enter, Space,
      and the arrow keys open the list. Arrow keys move, Home and End jump,
      typing finds a match, Enter picks, and Escape closes and returns focus to
      the trigger. The chosen item shows a check mark.
    </p>
    <p>
      The list fades and scales in over 120ms, and only fades when it lines up
      over the trigger. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested. In
      forced-colors mode the highlighted item gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Selects use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-input</code>, <code
        >--sprout-border</code
      >, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>, <code
        >--sprout-text</code
      >, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-focus</code>, <code
        >--sprout-danger</code
      >, <code>--sprout-shadow-control</code>, <code
        >--sprout-shadow-overlay</code
      >, and the control and panel radii. Only the focus ring follows the brand,
      so they look right with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark
      mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
